        "original_id": "b4dee71b-e23a-5f49-b002-588a0d6b178c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Keenan, Leofric\n- Works: The Exeter Book, Codex Exoniensis, Exeter Cathedral Library MS 3501\n- Organizations: Exeter Cathedral, Exeter Cathedral Library\n- Concepts: Anglo-Saxon texts, Anglo-Saxon poetry, the natural world\n\nFacts:\n- The Exeter Book, also known as the Codex Exoniensis and Exeter Cathedral Library MS 3501, is a tenth-century codex that anthologizes Anglo-Saxon poetry.\n- Leofric, the first bishop of Exeter, donated the Exeter Book to the library of Exeter Cathedral in 1072.\n- Paul Keenan's body of composition spans 27 years.\n- Paul Keenan's compositions consistently explore his fascination with Anglo-Saxon texts from The Exeter Book and the natural world.",
